  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global (Ghana, Kenya, Mauritius, Tanzania, Uganda, Bangladesh, Nepal, Indonesia, Sri Lanka, Thailand): Global RECAP: Global Regulatory and Fiscal Capacity Building Programme &#x2013; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Strengthened capacity of government officials, regulators, policymakers, academia and civil society to understand, develop and implement (as appropriate) regulatory and fiscal measures that promote healthy diets and physical activity. 2) Strengthened enabling environment on healthy diets and physical activity through national and international collaboration among policy makers, regulatory bodies, lawyers, public health and nutrition experts, civil society actors, academics, funders and communities. 3) Increased generation and use of relevant evidence and research from different disciplines to develop and implement effective regulatory and fiscal measures to promote healthy diets and physical activity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ministries and agencies responsible for legislative and regulatory responses to  non-communicable diseases, academic institutions, patient groups, health advocates, lawyers, national human rights commissions, community-based organizations, children&#x2019;s rights organizations, women&#x2019;s organizations, youth groups, labour groups, and faith communities, consumer organizations, and civil society organizations. Indirect beneficiaries: Individuals and their households, communities in programme countries at risk of noncommunicable diseases.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to strengthen national regulatory and fiscal environments to promote healthy diets and physical activity, contributing to the longer-term vision of reducing overweight/obesity and non-communicable diseases that are diet-related or related to insufficient physical activity.</narrative>
  </description>
